{
    "background_story": "Micah was a skilled artisan who spent most of his life mastering the ancient art of orphrey, a type of medieval embroidery. Growing up in a family of modest means, Micah's parents encouraged his creative talents, recognizing the value of his unique skillset. As a young man, Micah apprenticed with a renowned orphrey expert, learning the intricacies of gold thread and silk fabric. His exceptional talent soon earned him commissions from the local cathedral, where he created breathtaking works of art that adorned the altar cloths and vestments. Micah's orphrey pieces were not only stunning but also told stories of faith, hope, and redemption. His artistry brought solace to the community, and his reputation as a master orphrey artisan spread throughout the land.",
